# Digest 06: pattern 4, What should I get for this age?

Share: baby-development/_work/2026-11/digests-age-reread/share-06.md. Yes posts: 97. Near posts: 27.

## Pattern 4, share 06: yes posts

### The parent wants toys that hold the child's interest and keep being used.

10 of 97 posts.

Parents of two- and three-year-olds ask which toys will stay interesting, grow with the child or justify their space and cost. Some are replacing outgrown toys; others compare particular sets, sizes or track systems before buying. One parent wants winter activities, while another wants open-ended play that adults can enjoy too.

- "I'm trying to be more selective about what we buy for our 2.5-year-old because some of the bigger toys barely get touched anymore. We've had a few things he was really excited about at first, then a couple of weeks later they were mostly sitting there taking up space." [ar015-0088]
- "It's making me think twice before buying another big toy just because it looks fun in the moment. I'd rather have fewer things that actually stick around in his play." [ar015-0090]
- "My son is almost 4, we haven’t bought him any new toys in almost a year and I’m noticing he’s outgrown A LOT of the ones he has. Would love to know what your 3-4 year old boys are playing with that they love? We do have a ton of magna tiles and a few of the medium sized Lego kits which he enjoys, some hot wheels cars and small monster trucks." [ar068-0068]
- "I’m making a registry for my kids birthday and I really want to focus on quality toys that will last, allow for open ended play and encourage imagination, and preferably arent super loud and flashy. Bonus points if theyre also fun for the adults and Im not bored out of my mind playing with them 😛" [ar073-0097]
- "I mean specifically that brand? I’m debating one for my sons 3rd xmas. Also if you did would you recommend the 3-4 or the 4-7? He’s a big boy and is wearing 4t clothes at 2 right now." [ar038-0096]
- "Hey yall, thinking about diving into wood train set for Christmas but don’t really know where to start. I know that not ever brand tracks go with others and would like to hear input . My kid is 3. What brand track did you go with? What brand tracks also work with other brands ? Links or recommendations welcome !" [ar005-0092]

**But:** Having many toys does not ensure the child will play with them; one two-year-old prefers the parent's real activity. "My 2 year old has every toy I could think of to buy for a toddler but lately she doesn’t play with anything for too long. She’s MUCH more interested in what I’m doing." [ar044-0040]

