### The parent wants an age-suitable device or app for learning, stories or communication.

7 of 97 posts.

Parents consider apps, learning pads, audio story players and a phone for children aged two to almost four. Their requirements include avoiding ads or in-app payments, finding a step beyond a successful learning device and occupying an older child after a baby's arrival. Two requests concern accessibility: an audio player for a speech-delayed child with cochlear implants, and talk-to-text contact with a deaf grandfather.

- "I'm looking for toddler apps for my 2 year old that aren't going to show a bunch of advertisements or try to get them to make in app purchases. I have a few I really like primarily Toddleish for fun and Endless Alphabet for ABCs. She loves both of those but I wouldn't mind having a backup for variety. I don't mind paying a little up front but I really don't want ads or purchases while she's using it. Preferably options that are soothing and not hyper inducing or addictive." [ar079-0052]
- "Anyone have a recommendation of a good learning pad or another advanced leap frog they’ve had success with? Anything besides an actual tablet. Want to avoid those as long as we can. Possibly a little bigger screen. The one on the scribble and write is so dark and small." [ar061-0053]
- "Hi! So, I have 2 years old daughter, she is on speech delay. She has cochlear implants also. Do you think Yoto or Tonie box would be good for her? If yes, I can’t decide if I should get Yoto or Tonie box? […] My son is 9 months old, he is hearing. So, it would be good too?" [ar063-0069]
- "We want to reduce screen time but, with the arrival of a new baby we really need activities for her and we are thinking to put her iPad to use (which have been accumulating dust in a corner drawer). Any recommendations are highly appreciated!" [ar043-0137]
- "We are traveling across the country in a couple weeks and it’s my first time exposing my daughter to an iPad. She’s 2.5, I am trying to download some apps but some require we pay once you open it up. Does anyone have recommendations for free apps that are age appropriate that don’t require payment?" [ar047-0077]
- "Be kind. I never anticipated typing this. My dad is going deaf and he is my son’s best friend. We are considering a phone for my son so he can utilize a talk to text app and still communicate with his papa." [ar066-0132]

**But:** Wanting a screen limit can coexist with needing an activity now. "We want to reduce screen time but, with the arrival of a new baby we really need activities for her" [ar043-0137]

